# CVE-2026-31072: APScheduler RCE via insecure deserialization (CRITICAL)
# No fixed version available as of 2026-07-07.
# Risk mitigated: AsyncScheduler is used with in-memory store only (no persistent
# job store backend), so the deserialization attack vector is not exposed.
# Revisit when APScheduler 4.x releases a patched version.
CVE-2026-31072

# CVE-2026-25087: pyarrow DoS via use-after-free when reading IPC files (HIGH)
# Fixed in pyarrow 23.0.1, but pinning it causes a build dependency conflict.
# pyarrow is a transitive dep — not used directly. Revisit when upstream resolves.
CVE-2026-25087

# GHSA-6v7p-g79w-8964: msgpack 1.1.2 out-of-bounds read (HIGH)
# CVE-2025-47273: setuptools 70.3.0 path traversal (HIGH)
# Both are pip's own vendored internal dependencies (pip/_vendor/vendor.txt),
# not accessible to user code. pip 26.2.1 (latest) still ships these versions.
# Revisit when pip upstream updates its vendored copies.
GHSA-6v7p-g79w-8964
CVE-2025-47273

# CVE-2026-112940: filelock 3.32.7 arbitrary file overwrite via insecure
# database file reopening (HIGH)
# Risk mitigated: the advisory is specific to filelock's ReadWriteLock, which
# nothing in the dependency tree uses. huggingface-hub, litellm and tldextract
# are the only packages pulling filelock in, and all three contain zero
# references to ReadWriteLock — they use FileLock. Exploitation additionally
# requires a local attacker able to plant a symlink or journal file in the lock
# directory inside the container.
# Fixed in filelock 4.2.1, but the version is capped by upstream pins: adding
# filelock>=4.2.1 forces huggingface-hub 1.33.0 → 2.3.0 (a major bump) and
# downgrades litellm 1.106.4 → 1.103.9, which is not an acceptable trade for an
# unreachable code path.
# Scope note: this file is also loaded for the eval image, where the entry is
# inert — eval resolves filelock 4.2.4, outside the advisory's affected range
# (>= 3.20.4, <= 4.2.0), because nothing in that tree caps filelock. Only the
# base image is affected, and only because its newer litellm holds filelock at
# 3.x.
# Revisit when litellm allows filelock 4.x.
CVE-2026-112940
